/** User manual — IT & Cybersecurity edition: remote support contracts, reporting a security event, the ISO 27001 registers, marine cyber safety (IACS UR E26 / E27) and the purchases of the IT department.   GAS-CP-R97-085
 *  Every change to the menu group IT & Cybersecurity is described here, not in the Staff or Project Manager handbooks. */
return [
  'title' => 'Customer Portal — IT & Cybersecurity Handbook',
  'lede'  => 'How the menu group IT & Cybersecurity is used: remote support contracts, reporting a security event, the filing and reporting of ISO/IEC 27001 with its supplier evaluations and training, marine cyber safety for the products we supply (IACS UR E26 / E27) with the life cycle of their software, and the purchases of the IT department.',
  'sections' => [
    ['id' => 'where', 'title' => 'Where things are and who sees them', 'body' => [
      'The menu group IT & Cybersecurity stands on its own in the left menu, above Library. What you see in it depends on your account.',
      ['ul' => [
        'Remote support contracts — staff and customers; a customer sees the contracts of their own vessels.',
        'The quality / QHSE manager (a staff role named QHSE, HSE or Quality) has ISO 27001 and Marine cyber safety without being ticked in the team or in Access by position (v1.167.0).',
        'ISO 27001 — ISMS — management, administrators, the ISMS team, and everybody whose staff role or discipline is ticked under Access by position.',
        'Marine cyber safety (E26 / E27) — the same people, plus the programming team, who see this area only.',
        'Report a security event — every member of staff, including the accounts limited to HR or planning.',
      ]],
      'Access by position is a card on ISO 27001 — ISMS › Overview that only the CEO and the General Manager see and save. It lists every staff role and discipline with the number of active accounts; a tick gives all those people the ISO 27001 registers and Marine cyber safety. Until it is saved for the first time the portal ticks by name — top management and QHSE, project managers, IT, automation and electrical engineers — and the card says so.',
      'Two teams add single people who are not covered by their position: the ISMS team (ISO 27001 overview) has everything; the programming team (Marine cyber safety overview) has the marine area only. Management and administrators choose both teams and are the only ones who delete records.',
      ['tip' => 'Nothing that is filed in this group is sent to the assistant of the portal.'],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'remote', 'title' => 'Remote support contracts', 'body' => [
      'One contract per vessel and period: the hours included, the response time, the coverage hours and how we connect. Tickets raised on the vessel are covered by the live contract and every remote session is logged against it.',
      'An end date creates the renewal task, due the agreed number of days before the end; a contract without an end date is open-ended and has no renewal reminder.',
      'Stock per warehouse (v1.270.0): no database step. New page ?p=warehouse_stock and action dn_xfer_stock (warehouse right); a transfer of a whole warehouse runs in one transaction with a time limit of 180 seconds and at most 1200 lines per action.',
      'Delivery notes assembled from received lines (v1.269.0): database step install/migrate_cp_r97_281_dn_onward_from_lines.sql (check r9ac) — column src_line_id on inv_dn_lines. New page ?p=dn_forward (warehouse right) and action dn_forward; the quantities are checked again on the server inside one transaction, with the source notes locked.',
      'Delivery notes in the Service app (v1.268.0): database step install/migrate_cp_r97_280_dn_receiving_engineer_app.sql (check r9ab) — column to_user_id on inv_delivery_notes and the value app for accepted_via. New API routes for staff apps: GET /delivery-notes, GET /delivery-notes/{id}, GET /delivery-notes/{id}/pdf, POST /delivery-notes/{id}/decide — each answers only for notes addressed to the signed-in account or transfers to a warehouse it holds (404 otherwise); never for the customer app or Golden A/S Employee. The push for these notes goes to the Service app when the person has it and carries the route to the note. Service app web version 0.8.10; installed apps take it by themselves.',
      'Delivery notes — acceptance link, transfers, mobile warehouses (v1.267.0): database step install/migrate_cp_r97_279_dn_acceptance_transfer_mobile_wh.sql (check r9aa) — new columns on inv_warehouses, inv_delivery_notes and inv_dn_lines; new tables inv_dn_events (log), inv_dn_signs (signature of the recipient) and inv_dn_rsv (reservations that travelled with a transfer). Until the step is applied the module works as before: no transfer kind, no acceptance card. The public page customer/sign.php also serves the document kind dn — no new public route; the PDF of the note is made on request and only after the 6-digit code. Outgoing mail of the portal must be set up, as for service reports. A used link cannot answer a second time: the link is claimed in the database before the answer is stored.',
      'Georgian — ქართული (v1.265.0): Georgian is a new language of the portal; choose it in the language selector or on My account. The translation is delivered in stages. First stage: menu, sign-in, authenticator and passkeys, sessions and devices, dashboard, notifications, In / Out, planning and wellness. A text not translated yet is shown in English, so nothing is missing; each following stage replaces more of the English. The assistant answers in Georgian when the portal is set to Georgian. The apps follow in a later stage.',
      'Release updater — signed route and house-keeping (v1.261.2): (1) When the hosting server cannot be reached directly, a release is now installed through the website firewall. The update key is not sent: the deploy sends a signature made with the key that is valid for five minutes, for one use, and only for that release file and that action (verify, apply or status). The direct route with the key stays for the case where the server answers directly. (2) When the firewall cuts a long installation, the deploy asks the updater for its status until the run has finished and then reads its report. (3) House-keeping after every successful release: only the five newest backups (each holds the changed files and a full database dump) and the three newest applied release files are kept; release files uploaded and never applied are removed after one day. The numbers can be set in the server configuration (update › keep_backups, keep_zips). This frees the disk space that had built up release by release.',
      'Diagnostics after the health report of 26/11/2026 (v1.263.0): (1) Settings › System health › Slow pages: under «Start» a slow page now shows how long it waited for the session (another request of the same person still running) and how long it took to reach the database — shown when either is 100 ms or more; the same two figures are in the diagnostics and in the daily report. (2) The daily report is made by the clock job on the command line, where max_execution_time, opcache and the secure flag of the session cookie have other values than on the web server (0 s, off, off). The report now shows the values of the web server with the date they were read; they are read each time ▶ Run diagnostics is pressed in the browser. Until that is done once, the report says that they were not read yet. (3) The session is released while the portal waits for the assistant and taken again afterwards; after a wait of more than 20 seconds the database connection is tested and opened again when the server has closed it («MySQL server has gone away»). (4) The build date shown beside the version is set with every release again.',
      'Self-test through the website firewall — careful when the site is slow (v1.260.2): the daily test first asks the public address once; when it does not answer, or the firewall reports that the hosting does not answer (502 and above), the test stops there and Diagnostics shows «the public address does not answer — test not run», so that the test never adds requests to a site in trouble. The daily run is marked before it starts, so a slow run is never started a second time, and each request waits 5 seconds at most.',
      'Wider self-test through the website firewall (v1.260.1): the daily test and the Diagnostics row «Public pages through the website firewall» now cover ten doors: the acceptance link, the unsubscribe page, the sign-in address of the mobile apps, the careers form and the support / portal-access / newsletter form of goldenas.com.gr, and the pages of the five apps (Service, Golden PM, Golden HR, Employee, Customer). Each is called the way a browser or app calls it, without anything that could be written: the app sign-in without an app version, the forms without the site key. A door refused by the firewall, a page that sends no referrer, or a page that does not open is reported to the administrators with its name and the block ID.',
      'Self-test of the public pages through the website firewall (v1.260.0): (1) Once a day, after 07:00, the portal calls its own acceptance page and newsletter unsubscribe page through the public address, the way a phone browser does, with a link that does not exist (nothing is written). It checks that the pages answer, that they let the browser send the referrer, and that the website firewall lets a button through. (2) When a customer would be refused («Access Denied»), the administrators get the notification «Customers are refused on a public page of the portal» with the page and the block ID. (3) Settings › About › Diagnostics has the row «Public pages through the website firewall»: it runs the same test at once and shows the result; it also says whether the one-click «Unsubscribe» of Gmail and Outlook passes the firewall. If that is refused, put the path /customer/nl.php on the allowlist in the firewall settings (Firewall › Access control › Allow URL paths).',
      'Acceptance by e-mail link — «Access Denied» fixed (v1.259.1): a customer who opened the acceptance link of a service report (or of another document sent for acceptance) and pressed a button — send the code, confirm the code, accept or dispute — got the page «Access Denied – GoDaddy Website Firewall», block FBP007. The acceptance page told the browser to send no referrer, and the website firewall refuses every form sent without one. The page now sends the referrer to the portal only (never to other sites), so the buttons work; the same correction is on the newsletter unsubscribe page. A customer who met the error opens the same link again — nothing was lost and the link is still valid.',
      'Security — authenticator codes, obligatory authenticator, known devices (v1.259.0): (1) A wrong authenticator code typed in a mobile app counts toward the account lock like a wrong password: five wrong passwords or codes in a row lock the account for 15 minutes; the count goes back to zero only after a complete sign-in. (2) The authenticator is now obligatory by position for administrators and for the roles CEO, Managing Director, General Manager and every role with the Owner scope: the switch is set and stays set, the account cannot switch its authenticator off, the portal asks to set it up at the next sign-in, and the mobile apps refuse a new sign-in until it is set up in the portal (phones already signed in keep working). (3) My Account has the card «Devices that signed in to this account»: every browser and phone the account has used, first and last sign-in, the browser in use marked. «Forget» takes a device off the list so that its next sign-in is announced again; it does not sign the device out — «Sign out everywhere» does.',
      'Security — account lock from the apps, General Manager, new devices (v1.258.0): (1) Wrong passwords typed in a mobile app now count toward the account lock exactly as in the portal: five in a row, in the portal or in any app together, lock the account for 15 minutes, the administrators are notified and the entry «Locked out» appears in the login history with the app. A correct sign-in sets the count back to zero. (2) The authenticator is obligatory for the role «General Manager»: the switch «authenticator required» is set and stays set for every account with that role, the account cannot switch its authenticator off, the portal asks to set it up at the next sign-in, and the mobile apps refuse the sign-in of a General Manager until the authenticator is set up in the portal. (3) When the General Manager role is given to an account — in Portal accounts, by the accounts import, or by renaming a role to General Manager — the CEO gets a notification with the name, who did it and whether the account already has an authenticator. (4) New device notice: when an account signs in from a browser (browser and operating system) or a phone that it has not used before, the person gets the notification «New sign-in to your account» with the device and the address, and the advice to change the password and choose «Sign out everywhere» if it was not them. The devices used so far were written down at the update, so nobody is notified for the browser or phone already in use; the very first device of a new account is written down silently.',
      'Login history with the mobile apps (v1.257.0): (1) Settings › Login history now shows, for every entry, where it came from: the web portal, or the app (Service, Golden PM, Golden HR, Employee, Customer) with its version and the platform (iPhone / iPad, Android, browser). (2) Sign-ins of the apps were already recorded; now refused attempts in the apps (wrong password, locked account, wrong authenticator code) and the sign-out from an app are recorded too. (3) New filter «Where»: all mobile apps, one app, or the web portal; the search by name, e-mail or IP address works together with it, and the CSV export carries the three new columns. Passkey sign-ins have their own outcome labels and count in the figures of the last 24 hours. (4) In «Portal usage» every person has two new columns: the number of app sign-ins in the period (a link to those entries) and, per app, when it was last used. (5) Entries made before this version show «Web portal» when they came from the portal and carry no app name when they came from an app.',
      'The log of a document is folded (v1.198.2): the card "Log" (also named "History" or "Audit trail") at the bottom of a document page — purchase order, requisition, BOM, supplier invoice and payment request, production order, system budget, offer, ticket, timesheet, job order, activity report, task, ISO / IT record, assessment, recruitment application — is now closed when the page opens, so the page is shorter. Click the title (the + on the right) to open it; nothing is removed and everything is still recorded as before.',
      'Speed — Dashboard, KPIs, Cash flow, projects list and HR pages (v1.198.1): the health report of 19 November showed the Dashboard taking up to four seconds with about 4 300 database statements whenever the KPI cockpit was renewed, and the projects list and the HR dashboard asking several hundred. The cause was that the budget and KPI figures were asked sub-project by sub-project (13 statements each). They are now read for all sub-projects together in about a dozen statements, and the same was done for the per-project figures of the projects list (offers, footprint, open tickets, permits), the KPI trends, the cash-flow forecast, the people online, and the people list of the HR pages (it was read up to fifteen times per page). Nothing changes in what the pages show — the numbers were compared before and after and are identical. In the test copy with 150 projects the Dashboard went from about 6 400 statements to about 220, KPIs and the KPI report from about 8 000 and 6 300 to about 100, Cash flow from 2 600 to 60, and the projects list was halved. The remaining lines of "Slow statements" are single simple statements that waited on the hosting database for 0,1–0,3 s; they are not caused by the portal. The line "[ar_old] … made internal" under PHP errors is an information message of the report filing, not an error.',
      'Filters — type to pick from the list (v1.195.3): a drop-down became a type-to-search list only when it had more than eight entries, so a short filter such as Vessel on the purchase orders opened as a plain list. Now, in every filter bar of the portal, a drop-down with four or more entries opens with a search box: click it, type a few letters, press Enter or click the entry. The Vessel and Supplier filters of Purchase orders and of the Pipeline board are always searchable, whatever their length. Fixed choices of two or three entries (for example Purpose) stay plain lists.',
      'Equipment given to employees (v1.189.0): the members of the IT & Cybersecurity team have HR › Equipment to give. Choose the employee and prepare what he or she receives from IT — computer, telephone / SIM, keys / cards / badge; hardware of the asset inventory can be picked from the list (description and number are filled in, and one asset cannot be given to two people). HR is notified and puts your lines on the issue list the employee accepts. You see only the lines of your categories, not the HR card. The asset record then shows "held by …"; when the employee hands the equipment back and HR accepts it, the asset is free again.',
      'Daily health report — three corrections (v1.177.1): (1) "Database steps: GAS-CP-R46-005" was a false alarm of the check itself — the step had been applied; it now reads the column correctly. (2) "Update backups": the daily house-keeping keeps the last three backup folders and now really removes the older ones (they contain sub-folders, which the old clean-up could not empty); the warning disappears after the next night. (3) Slow pages: the Projects list ran several thousand database statements per view because of per-sub-project calculations; see the line "statements per page" of the next reports to follow the effect.',
      'Subscriptions (v1.167.0): a contract is also the subscription of the customer. Besides the period it carries the product (Mb Connect, FortiGate …) with its serial number, the renewal period (1 year, 3 years …), the date installed, the payment status (Ongoing, Pending payment, Paid by customer, Rejected by customer, Subscription expired), the licence expiry of the device and the SQ / offer number it was sold with.',
      'What runs out: the five numbers above the list — active subscriptions (with those pending payment), renewal within 30 days, renewal within 90 days, licences running out within 90 days, and expired and not renewed — open the list filtered. The list has a column Licence expiry; a date within 90 days is gold, a passed one red. The status filter adds Renewal within 90 days, Licence runs out within 90 days and To renew — no renewal offer yet.',
      'Import: under the filters, Import subscriptions from the list of Sales takes the .csv or .xlsx with the columns Vessel, SQ, Product, Subscription details, Payment Status, Renewal Period, Renewal Date, Date Installed, Price, Serial Number, Expiry Date. The vessel is found by its name (M/Y, S/Y … ignored; former names count); tick Create the vessels that are not in the portal to add missing ones, otherwise those rows are listed and skipped. A row without a vessel is skipped. Rejected by customer becomes Cancelled, Subscription expired or a renewal date in the past becomes Expired, everything else Active with its renewal task. A subscription already there (same vessel, SQ and product) is skipped, so the file can be uploaded again. Imported subscriptions are internal — set Visibility to the customer on those the customer should see. Import, renewal offer and renewal are for administrators, management and staff who see the offers.',
      'Sales: the subscription page has a block Sales — the offer it was sold with (linked when the SQ or offer number is among the offers of the portal) and the renewal offer. + Renewal offer, with a project of the vessel chosen, creates a draft offer in Commercial › Offers titled Renewal — plan — vessel (period), with the fee of the subscription as amount and the new period in the notes; complete and send it there — from then on it stands in the sales pipeline. The offer page shows the subscription it belongs to. When the customer accepts, Renew for another period moves the end date forward by the renewal period, sets the payment status to Ongoing, makes the renewal offer the offer of the subscription and writes a line in the internal notes; the renewal task moves with the new end date.',
      'Weekly e-mail to Sales (v1.168.0): once a week, from Monday, the people marked Sales (Settings › Users) and management receive by e-mail and as a notification the subscriptions to renew — running out within 90 days or lapsed in the last 180 days, with the renewal offer if there is one — and the licences running out within 90 days. Nothing is sent in a week when nothing runs out; accounts without financial data are left out. Under the filters of the list, Weekly e-mail to Sales shows whether it is on, with Send now; management turns it off or on there.',
      'Serial numbers (v1.168.0): the serial number of a device is shown to Golden A/S staff only — a customer sees the product, the period and the licence expiry of their subscriptions, not the serial number, and cannot search by it.',
      'Commercial › Pipeline lists Subscriptions to renew: those running out within 90 days or lapsed in the last 180 days that the customer did not refuse, with the renewal offer and its status, or the button to raise it.',
      'The page moved here from Library in v1.159.0.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'report', 'title' => 'Reporting a security event', 'body' => [
      'Anything that looks wrong for the security of information is reported at once: a suspicious e-mail that was opened, a lost laptop or phone, a password that may have been given away, an unknown USB stick, a door left open, data sent to the wrong person. It is better to report something harmless than to miss something serious.',
      ['ol' => [
        'Open IT & Cybersecurity › Report a security event.',
        'Write what it is in a few words, when it happened, what is affected and what happened — what you saw and what you did. Never write a password.',
        'Send the report. It is filed as an incident with status Reported and the ISMS team and the administrators are notified at once.',
      ]],
      ['tip' => 'Do not delete the e-mail or the file concerned and do not switch the device off unless you are told to.'],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'isms', 'title' => 'ISO 27001 — the overview and the registers', 'body' => [
      'ISO 27001 — ISMS opens on the overview: documents approved, controls implemented out of those that apply, open risks by level, open incidents and open nonconformities; the table of registers with records, open and overdue; Needs attention (a due date passed or a review date reached); the planned audits and reviews; the ISMS team.',
      'Each tab is a register, tied to its clause of ISO/IEC 27001:2022:',
      ['ul' => [
        'Documents (7.5) — policies, procedures and records with version, approval and next review. It starts with the items of documented information the standard asks for, as drafts; attach the approved file to each. The five governance documents of the company carry their own numbers and their titles in English and Greek, as approved by the CEO on 01/08/2026 with the next review on 01/08/2027: ISMS-MAN-001 ISMS Manual, ISMS-TIER1-001 Information Security Policy, ISMS-TIER1-002 ISMS Scope Statement, ISMS-TIER1-003 Information Security Roles & Responsibilities and ISMS-TIER1-004 Risk Assessment & Treatment Methodology. Attach to each of them the Greek original and the English translation under Files.',
        'Risks (6.1.2 · 8.2 · 8.3) — asset, threat, vulnerability, likelihood (1 Rare, 2 Unlikely, 3 Possible, 4 Likely, 5 Almost certain) and impact (1 Negligible, 2 Minor, 3 Moderate, 4 Major, 5 Severe), the treatment and its plan, and the residual likelihood and impact. The level follows the risk matrix of the methodology ISMS-TIER1-004 and has four steps — Low, Medium, High, Critical: an impact of 5 is at least High whatever the likelihood, and Critical from a likelihood of 3. Acceptance: Low by the risk owner; Medium with review and approval of the IT Manager; High is treated as a rule and accepted only by exception with the risk owner and the IT Manager, and reported to the management review; Critical is treated or formally escalated to management — the IT Manager alone cannot accept it. A risk without likelihood and impact counts as not scored on the overview.',
        'Interested parties (4.2) — who they are (owners, customers, employees, suppliers, authorities and class, certification body), what they need and expect, and how it is met.',
        'Statement of Applicability (6.1.3 d) — the 93 controls of Annex A. For each: applicable or not with the justification, how far it is implemented, how it is met, and the evidence attached.',
        'Assets (A 5.9) — type, classification, location and criticality.',
        'Incidents (A 5.24 – 5.28) — what happened, severity, containment, root cause, lessons learned and who was notified. Reports from staff arrive here.',
        'Audits & reviews (9.2 · 9.3) — internal audits, management reviews, reviews of access rights, backup restore tests and continuity exercises, with result and report.',
        'Nonconformities (10.2) — source, cause, correction, corrective action and the check of its effectiveness.',
        'Objectives (6.2) — measure, target and result.',
        'Suppliers and Supplier evaluations (A 5.19 – 5.22) — see the next section.',
        'Training & awareness (7.2 · 7.3) — see the section on training.',
        'Legal requirements (A 5.31) — the obligation and how it is met.',
      ]],
      'A record: every record is numbered automatically — a new record opens with its number already filled in (ISMS-033, RSK-001, INC-001 …; a document or a software release of a product and an evaluation of a supplier are numbered under it: CBS-001-D11, CBS-001-SW01, SUP-003-E01) and you may type another number as long as it is not used in the register; remote support contracts are numbered GAS-RS-year-number in the same way. Besides the number a record has a title, a status, an owner, a due date and a next review, the fields of its register, files and a history. Save the record first; then attach the evidence (PDF, Office, images, e-mail, zip, up to 25 MB each) with a note of what it is. The history keeps who created it, which fields changed, every status step and every file attached or removed.',
      'Import from Excel: on the list of a register press Import template, fill one record per row and upload it with Import Excel; a code or a title already in the register is skipped. The suppliers of ISO 27001 can be imported too — choose the supplier of the supplier list on the record afterwards. The Statement of Applicability is filled the same way: its Import template is the list of the 93 controls as they stand — fill Status, Next review, Justification and How it is met; each row is matched by the number of its control (A 5.1 … A 8.34) and fills that control. A control that somebody already worked on (status changed or a text entered) is left as it is, so the file can be uploaded again safely. Registers that hang under another record (evaluations, documents and releases of a product) and the approved suppliers of QHSE are not imported this way.',
      'Lists are filtered by word, status and owner, and by Open or Overdue. Open means that the record still needs work; overdue that its due date has passed or its review date has come.',
      'Reminders: the owner of a record is notified 14 days before a due date or a review date; a record without an owner goes to the ISMS team.',
      'All registers (Excel) at the top gives one workbook with a summary and a sheet per register — the file for the auditor.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'suppliers', 'title' => 'Suppliers and their evaluation', 'body' => [
      'A record of the supplier register is a supplier of Procurement › Suppliers. Choose it from the list — a supplier is in the register once and its name becomes the title — and state the service, the access it has to our information, how critical it is and the agreement (contract, NDA, DPA). A new supplier starts as To evaluate.',
      ['ol' => [
        'On the supplier record press + New evaluation and choose the kind: initial (before first use), periodic, or after an incident.',
        'Score the six criteria from 1 (very weak) to 5 (very good): agreement in place; certification and evidence (ISO 27001 or equivalent); control of access to our information and systems; incidents and how they are reported to us; continuity and reliability of the service; quality and response.',
        'Write any conditions asked from the supplier and attach the questionnaire or the certificate received.',
        'Set the evaluation to Done. All six scores are needed; the date and the evaluator are filled in when empty.',
      ]],
      'The rating is the sum of the scores in percent. The result is proposed from it — 70 % and more Approved, 50 to 69 % Approved with conditions, below 50 % Not approved — and another result can be chosen.',
      'The latest finished evaluation gives the supplier its rating and its state (Active, Approved with conditions, Not approved) and dates the next evaluation: 12 months later when the supplier is critical (4 or 5) or reaches confidential or personal information, otherwise 24 months. The owner is reminded 14 days before.',
      'People of the ISMS also see the card Information security (ISO 27001) on the page of the supplier in Procurement: the state, the rating and the next evaluation, or a button that adds the supplier to the register.',
      ['tip' => 'The register is for the suppliers that handle our information or our systems — not for the whole supplier list.'],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'training', 'title' => 'Training and awareness, kept in the personnel records', 'body' => [
      'An ISO 27001 training is recorded once and kept in HR, so that it appears in the personnel record of everybody who attended.',
      ['ol' => [
        'Create the record in Training & awareness: title, planned date, audience and trainer.',
        'On the record, in the card HR › Training and personnel records, press Create in HR › Training — or link a training that HR has already published.',
        'After the session tick who attended and press Save attendance. Tick Set the training to Done to close the record here and the training in HR together.',
      ]],
      'The attendance is written to HR › Training and shows on the Training tab of each personnel record; somebody who was marked as attended and is un-ticked becomes absent. HR adds certificates and scores there. The number of attendees of the ISO record follows the ticks.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'marine', 'title' => 'Marine cyber safety — IACS UR E26 / E27', 'body' => [
      'Marine cyber safety (E26 / E27) holds the computer-based systems we supply in our projects, the documents IACS UR E27 asks for each of them, their approval by the classification society and every release of their software.',
      'Equipment: add the equipment and choose its vessel, project and sub-project (a sub-project fills in its project, a project its vessel), the classification society, the approval route (plan approval per vessel or type approval), the system category of UR E22 and whether it has an interface to an untrusted network; record the class reference and the certificate with its validity. The status follows the approval: In preparation → Submitted to class → Class comments → Approved → In service → Retired.',
      'Equipment, not products (v1.169.0): the records of Marine cyber safety are called Equipment, as in the Equipment register, and a record can carry the serial number it is about. On the record choose Serial number (Equipment register) — the equipment we produced or sold that is not yet in cyber safety; one record per serial number, and the vessel of the serial number is taken over when none is chosen. From the other side, the page of a serial number (Equipment) shows a card Marine cyber safety with the status, the class, the documents approved and the software version — or the button + Add to Marine cyber safety, which creates the record with its ten UR E27 documents, the vessel and, when the serial number came from a production order, its project and sub-project. The overview lists under To add — production orders under UR E26 / E27 the serial numbers that have no record yet, each with the same button.',
      'Which production orders (v1.170.0): only the orders marked Cyber safety approval (IACS UR E26 / E27) are listed. The tick is on the production order (Fleet › Equipment › Production, New / Edit order) and is set by whoever raises or manages the order when its equipment is a computer-based system that has to comply; the order then carries the mark UR E26 / E27, the change is written in its log and the programming team and the ISMS team are told. Orders without the tick never appear in Marine cyber safety. A serial number can still be chosen by hand on an equipment record or added from its own page.',
      'UR E27 documentation: every new piece of equipment receives the ten documents of UR E27 section 3.1 as Missing —',
      ['ol' => [
        'CBS asset inventory',
        'Topology diagrams',
        'Description of security capabilities',
        'Test procedure of security capabilities',
        'Security configuration guidelines',
        'Secure development lifecycle documents',
        'Plans for maintenance and verification of the CBS',
        'Information supporting the owner\'s incident response and recovery plan',
        'Management of change plan',
        'Test reports',
      ]],
      'Give each its document number and revision, attach every issued revision and move it: Draft → Internal review → Submitted to class → Approved, or Class comments with the comments written in. A document that does not apply is set to Not applicable. Further documents are added with + on the equipment.',
      'Software releases: every version of the software of a piece of equipment is a record — version, component (PLC program, HMI, SCADA, firmware, network configuration, operating system), kind of change, what changed and why, change request, repository tag or archive location, SHA-256 of the released package, who tested it and the test report, whether the classification society must be notified, the rollback plan. It moves Development → Test → Review → Approved → Released → Installed on board, and later Superseded or Withdrawn.',
      ['ul' => [
        'A release is approved by somebody other than its developer (management and administrators excepted). The approver and the date are recorded automatically.',
        'A release cannot be set to Released or Installed before it is approved.',
        'Going back to Development or Test withdraws the approval.',
        'A release sent to Review notifies the programming team, the ISMS team and the administrators; the developer is told when it is approved, released, installed or withdrawn.',
      ]],
      'The overview shows per piece of equipment the approval, the documents approved out of those that apply and the software version on board; the releases waiting for approval; those approved but not yet installed; and the certificates that expire within 90 days.',
      'The equipment also appears on the page of its vessel and on the first tab of its sub-project, where + New equipment starts one that is already linked. Lists are filtered by equipment, vessel and project. Products, documents, releases (Excel) gives the workbook for the surveyor or the customer.',
      ['tip' => 'Source code and packages are not stored in the portal — only their reference and checksum, so that the copy installed on board can be verified.'],
